<title>INDIA: INDIA CRISIL DOWNGRADES ORIENT PRESS.</title>
<headline>INDIA CRISIL DOWNGRADES ORIENT PRESS.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Credit Rating Information Services of India Ltd (CRISIL) said it had downgraded to BB the the A- ratings it had assigned to the 100-million-rupee and 70-million-rupee non-convertible debenture programmes of Orient Press Limited (OPL).</p>
<p>The new rating indicates a moderate safety of timely payment of interest and principal, CRISIL said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Newsroom (91) 22 265 9000; (91) 264 1699</p>
